// submits without any visible frontend crash. Frontend layer looks clean
// so far - proceed to the Network tab.

// STEP 2 - Network tab: The PATCH request to /api/profile shows:
//   Request body: { "name": "Updated Name" }
//   Response status: 200
//   Response body: { "success": true, "data": { "name": "Updated Name" } }
// This is suspicious - the response CLAIMS success with the correct data.
// This rules out an obvious frontend or backend logic bug in this specific
// request/response pair - proceed to checking the actual stored data.

